<Solution>
  <!--
    Why this file exists, and it is NOT primarily about building.

    `ensure-built.ps1` builds each csproj by explicit path and never reads a solution, so nothing in the build
    needed this. What needs it is WORKSPACE ANCHORING.

    PipeKey.FindRepositoryRoot walks up from a file looking for a `.git` marker, and falls back to the outermost
    `.sln`/`.slnx` it passed. When nothing above a file is a repository it returns null, and ResolveWorkspaceRoot
    then answers the STARTING DIRECTORY — so a marker-less tree mints one Roslyn daemon PER SUBDIRECTORY someone
    opens a file in. That is documented on FindRepositoryRoot itself: "editing two files in two subdirectories of
    one marker-less tree produced two daemons."

    This repository is a git checkout, so it anchors fine. ITS INSTALLED COPY DOES NOT. Claude copies the plugin
    into ~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-roslyn-lsp/roslyn/<version>/, and a copy carries no `.git`. Measured
    2026-09-09 across 84 daemon logs, three daemons had been minted inside that cache at SUBDIRECTORY roots:

        ...\plugins\cache\claude-roslyn-lsp\roslyn\0.1.1\bridge
        ...\plugins\cache\claude-roslyn-lsp\roslyn\0.1.1\client
        ...\plugins\cache\claude-roslyn-lsp\roslyn\0.1.0\daemon

    Three separate Roslyn instances to read one plugin's own source, because a browsed subdirectory of an
    unmarked copy IS a workspace by that rule. A solution file at the plugin root ships WITH the copy, so the
    cache anchors at <version>/ and the whole plugin is one workspace wherever it is installed.

    The by-construction fix is a marker the existing rule already honours, not a new special case in PipeKey:
    teaching the resolver about plugin manifests would add a second anchoring concept to maintain, and this uses
    the one that is there. It also improves the checkout: the daemon logged "no solution found; opening 7
    project(s)" for this repo and can now open one solution instead.

    Keep every project listed. A project missing here is invisible to the workspace even though it builds.
  -->
  <Configurations>
    <Platform Name="Any CPU" />
    <Platform Name="x64" />
  </Configurations>
  <Project Path="bridge/ClaudeRoslynLsp.Bridge.csproj" />
  <Project Path="cli/ClaudeRoslynLsp.Cli.csproj" />
  <Project Path="client/ClaudeRoslynLsp.Client.csproj" />
  <Project Path="daemon/ClaudeRoslynLsp.Daemon.csproj" />
  <Project Path="extensions-api/ClaudeRoslynLsp.Extensions.Abstractions.csproj" />
  <Project Path="mcp/ClaudeRoslynLsp.Mcp.csproj" />
  <Folder Name="/samples/">
    <Project Path="samples/SampleRunningSystemExtension/SampleRunningSystemExtension.csproj" />
  </Folder>
</Solution>
